<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "published": true,
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-04-15T14:49:37.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 22366,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "panels": [
      {
        "text": "",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/6ce79bce9245fbf186cac4d0309cf388-Teaching Moves_ Facilitating Capstone Projects.png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-ee5adfcb-0be1-4b19-bb31-a1e94eee71ba",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Group Challenges\n\nGroup capstone projects are powerful, but they come with predictable challenges.\n\nThis tutorial presents common classroom scenarios and simple teacher moves to help you facilitate **collaboration, maintain focus, and support meaningful student work**.\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/6630df28b66d84b6c4012d4a6836db4d-Teaching Moves_ Facilitating Capstone Projects (1).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-2267017e-0c57-4439-907c-f71b4a6dde78",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Scenario (Before)\n\nYou notice one student taking over as Project Leader...assigning tasks, correcting others, and making decisions without team input. \n\nOther students are disengaging or just waiting to be told what to do.\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/9e66e4fa616cbb3aa9bfa1d64180f7b5-Capstone Projects.png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-429d4798-f047-4436-ba4d-7162c6af017c",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Teacher Move \nRedirect the student away from being “the boss” and back to the process.\n\n**Ask:** “What does your Kanban board say you should be working on next?”\n**Then follow with:** “How can your team use that to decide together?”\n\nThis shifts leadership from authority to facilitation and keeps decisions grounded in shared planning tools, not personalities.\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/df26a3b5ce0b97c373f997f0a86d8709-Capstone Projects (1).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-02e38e56-d447-4fb5-9445-19fe591d751e",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Scenario (Before)\n\nOn Day 2, teams jump straight into building (designing screens, picking colors, or starting code) without clearly explaining how their app is supposed to work. \n\nWhen you ask questions, their ideas are vague or inconsistent.\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/867c23bc74a237b325d03344ca82886d-Capstone Projects (2).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-a297eb00-9b03-403c-af21-dfc87ef8bbd5",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Teacher Move \n\nPause the group and require clarity before progress.\n**Ask:** “Walk me through one user interaction. What does the user do, and what happens next?”\n\nIf they can’t explain it clearly, they’re not ready to build.\nThis reinforces that planning and system thinking come before coding, not after.\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/f25547f1ea9273b5106c2c69f2f597ae-Capstone Projects (3).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-98aaef4a-e69c-4c94-9d3d-465e33438b09",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Scenario (Before)\n\nTeams keep adding new ideas (extra screens, features, or “cool” elements), but their core app is incomplete or buggy. \n\nThey’re excited, but their project is becoming scattered and unfinished.\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/46e52f6468973ba9d05cb528cf110074-Capstone Projects (4).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-928cbfd2-b981-4540-a5ff-0785b3359e82",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Teacher Move \n\nSlow them down and refocus on purpose.\n\n**Ask:**\n- “What problem does this feature solve?”\n- “What testing or feedback led you to add it?”\n\n**Then remind them**: a simpler, well-explained app is stronger than a complex, unfinished one.\n\nThis helps students prioritize intentional design over quantity.\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d81b980355b44b21683334706ead8860-Capstone Projects (5).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-00868d1b-6904-4bf1-be94-dcbd0a07464c",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Scenario (Before)\n\nStudents don’t know how their projects will be shared, so some overbuild while others under-prepare. \n\nAt the end, expectations feel unclear or mismatched.\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/ed2aa58acf4d019b3076e11fa159682f-Capstone Projects (6).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-1e491800-b256-4cc7-b4dc-fcfcaa0fdc69",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Teacher Move \n\n Set expectations early and frame the purpose.\n Tell students upfront how they will share:\n- Option 1: In-class gallery walk\n- Option 2: School/community showcase\n- Option 3: Public/online sharing\n\nExplain that the goal is to celebrate their thinking and decisions, not just the final product.\nThis helps students scope their work appropriately and reduces unnecessary stress.\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d5c493c9d214a993762046a74b194164-Capstone Projects (7).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-6cedd9ca-2b57-41bb-90b2-99b04ef52564",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Facilitating Confident Capstones\n\nGuide students to:\n- Use shared tools like the Kanban board\n- Think before they build\n- Focus on meaningful features\n- Understand how their work will be shared\n\nYour role isn’t to manage every decision, it’s to create the conditions where students can **collaborate, reflect, and confidently explain their thinking.**\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d33e52b5c1ce86a7dc729ffce2e6070f-Teaching Moves_ Facilitating Capstone Projects (10).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U6-class-mgmt-12-b5ae8528-4ed9-4b80-9f0e-b0c951bd8737",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      }
    ],
    "name_suffix": "_2025-pilot"
  },
  "audit_log": "[{\"changed_at\":\"2026-04-15T14:49:37.619+00:00\",\"changed\":[\"cloned from \\\"pl-aif-2-U5-steps-music-app-panal\\\"\"],\"cloned_from\":\"pl-aif-2-U5-steps-music-app-panal\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-04-23 15:01:13 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"panels\"],\"changed_by_id\":19028,\"changed_by_email\":\"amanda.dennard@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-04-23 15:03:22 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"panels\"],\"changed_by_id\":19028,\"changed_by_email\":\"amanda.dennard@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-04-23 15:05:09 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"panels\"],\"changed_by_id\":19028,\"changed_by_email\":\"amanda.dennard@code.org\"}]"
